-- Companion spells from the vanity collection (VanityCollection.dbc, mostly the "Sigil of ..." boss
-- companions) summon creatures with no creature_template row. AscensionCollectionModelData.h answers the
-- client's creature query for them, so they show a name and a model in the pet window, but
-- Creature::InitEntry needs a template, so the summon itself fails. These rows let them be summoned.
-- Names and displays are the collection model table's (hertigservices/ascension-data creature cache).
-- Model scales follow the companion rule of rev_20261009_60_companion_scale.sql: the model's bounding box
-- in the client's CreatureModelData/CreatureDisplayInfo is at most 1.2 yd tall and 1.8 yd long; models
-- without a bounding box keep scale 1.
